OneiOS, stack 555b13d (NativeMetal 935c468), patches-555b13d/NativeMetal/0002: OneiOS's boot-argument switches for what the
base does itself, and the idle tick.
Upstream: none (OneiOS). On the stack 624bab3 these features were OneiOS's ports (patches/NativeMetal/0002 and 0004,
patches/metal2vulkan/0001 and 0008), each with its switch; NativeMetal 935c468 has the features (46fdc91/935c468's idle timer,
0e7550a's pacing and read wait, bridge patches 0040's YCbCr planes and 0041's makings on the asking thread) and no boot argument
for most of them. This keeps the names the images and the documents already use:
  oneios-idle-trim=0     ONEIOS_IDLE_TRIM=0: no 2 s idle trim timer (watchIdleMemory)
  (the idle tick)        each tick of that timer calls oneios_idle_tick where the image has it (weak; Switches-555b13d.inc:
                         Turnip's freed-BO cache trimmed once a minute, patches-555b13d/mesa/0001)
  oneios-read-wait=0     ONEIOS_READ_WAIT=0: the render server does not ask the kernel to wait for other processes' writers
                         (take20's -readwait0 image); the base's own A/B is the file /private/var/ngpu/debug/no-surface-sync
  oneios-sched-pace=0    ONEIOS_SCHED_PACE=0: command buffers scheduled at submission; the base's own A/B is the file
                         /private/var/ngpu/debug/no-scheduled-pacing (and scheduled-depth)
  oneios-ycbcr-planes=0  the base's gpu-ycbcr-planes=0 (NATIVE_METAL_YCBCR_PLANES=0): every two-plane YCbCr surface texture
                         with its converted image, in every process (the base makes them over their planes alone in every
                         process; take18 did so in backboardd only)
  oneios-compile-here=0  no METAL2VULKAN_COMPILE_ON_ASKING_THREAD=1: a driver pipeline is made on a thread the runtime starts
                         for it. CHANGED DEFAULT: the base sets it in every process (on); take18's plug-in was off without
                         oneios-compile-here=1
Removable: yes (ONEIOS_METAL_SKIP=base-features-switches): the switches above then do nothing, and Turnip's freed-BO cache is
no longer trimmed at idle (nothing calls oneios_idle_tick).
Tested: applies. First compiled by the CI. Not run on a phone.

